decision_conditions:
Condition : 4 - Before the relevant part of the work is begun, detailed drawings and specifications of external materials and architectural details, as appropriate, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. The following details are required:

a) Detailed drawings (minimum scale 1:10) of all new external joinery, including replacement sash windows, new lower ground floor entrance door, french doors and any associated joinery, including sections, frame dimensions, materials, finish and colour;

b) Detailed drawings (minimum scale 1:10) of the proposed front railings, gates, half wall and rear Juliet balcony balustrades, including sections, height, design, finish and colour;

c) Detailed drawings (minimum scale 1:10) of the proposed rear Juliet balcony balustrades, including sections, height, design, finish and colour;

d) Details and samples of the facing materials of the side extension, including brickwork;

d) Detailed drawings (minimum scale 1:10) of the proposed side extension rooflights, including upstand dimensions, finish and external appearance.

Reason: To ensure that the external appearance of the building is satisfactory and that it preserves the character and appearance of the conservation area in accordance with policies D1 and D2 of the Camden Local Plan 2017 and policies DH1 and DH2 of the Hampstead Neighbourhood Plan 2025.
